# MyChat coding practices

## Style

- Prefer small, named functions; factories when a module needs DOM/memory callbacks.
- Keep imports at the top of the file (no inline imports).
- Match existing naming: `createX`, `runChat` / `runImage`, `setStatus`, `persistSession`.
- Escape user/tool HTML (`escapeHtml`); Markdown goes through `renderMarkdown` (DOMPurify + `target=_blank`).
- Use `isAbortError` / `StoppedError` for cancel paths; never swallow abort as a normal failure.

## Product contracts

- Think (`think: true`) only for models in `THINK_MODELS` (today: `qwen3.5:9b`).
- Auto-scroll the thread only when near bottom (`scrollThreadToBottom`).
- Persist session after meaningful turns; on quota, retry without image payloads.
- Clear conversation must keep facts & RAG; say so in UI copy.
- External links open in a new tab (`noopener noreferrer`).

## When changing flows

- Update Settings toggles + `config.js` keys together if you add memory/chat options.
- Extend `js/memory/*` behind the orchestrator facade; UI should keep talking to `prepareTurn` / settings, not raw stores.
- After navigation / primary CTA / memory / tool UX changes, keep or add coverage under `test/` and run `npm test`.

## ❌ Avoid

- Purple/glow “AI slop” restyles; keep the cream + violet/magenta token set in `css/tokens.css`
- `waitForTimeout`-style brittle waits in any future UI tests — assert roles/text/URL
- Broad drive-by refactors unrelated to the request
